    <string name="intro_title">Before you talk</string>
    <string name="intro_ok">Got it</string>
    <string name="intro_body">Blip is a chat and a walkie-talkie. There is no account. The name stays on this phone.\n\nThe channel is where you write. The radio is where you talk, like a Zello: hold the button, speak, let go. Everyone on the channel hears that voice.\n\nPhones nearby pass the voice along, even with no internet. If nobody is close enough to pass it on, it goes over the internet instead.\n\nA direct chat is private. Only the other phone can open it. A room with a password is private to the people who know it.\n\nThe public channel, place rooms, and rooms without a password can be read by anyone who receives them. Your name can be seen too. What is saved on this phone is not locked.\n\nBlip opens in English. The language is in Settings.\n\nInternet and local keeps looking for phones nearby and also uses the internet.\n\nInternet only does not look for phones nearby. The talk goes over the internet.\n\nPlace rooms stay nearby. They do not go over the internet. If the internet path is down, messages wait.</string>
